From: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: free ispecs only after the handshake workqueues are drained

wg_destruct() frees the junk packet specs before destroy_workqueue(),
so a handshake send worker still running on another CPU can dereference
spec->pkt / spec->mods after they were freed (upstream issue #139).

Move the jp_spec_free() loop below the destroy_workqueue() calls, where
no worker can be running any more. The remaining fixes from the original
version of this patch (mutex_init moved to wg_newlink, freeing old
pkt/mods on re-setup, resetting sizes before the fill loop, freeing desc)
were taken upstream in v3.0.

Signed-off-by: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/device.c b/src/device.c
index 84d63d8..2fa0008 100644
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -272,9 +272,6 @@ static void wg_destruct(struct net_device *dev)
 	struct wg_device *wg = netdev_priv(dev);
 	int i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(wg->ispecs); ++i)
-		jp_spec_free(&wg->ispecs[i]);
-
 	rtnl_lock();
 	list_del(&wg->device_list);
 	rtnl_unlock();
@@ -287,6 +284,11 @@ static void wg_destruct(struct net_device *dev)
 	destroy_workqueue(wg->handshake_receive_wq);
 	destroy_workqueue(wg->handshake_send_wq);
 	destroy_workqueue(wg->packet_crypt_wq);
+	/* Free junk packet specs after all workqueues are drained, so no send
+	 * worker can race with jp_spec_free().
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(wg->ispecs); ++i)
+		jp_spec_free(&wg->ispecs[i]);
 	wg_packet_queue_free(&wg->handshake_queue, true);
 	wg_packet_queue_free(&wg->decrypt_queue, false);
 	wg_packet_queue_free(&wg->encrypt_queue, false);
